<BaseLayout title="Process Improvement & Business Operations" current="/process-improvement/" description="Process improvement, SOP program leadership, reporting, quality control, systems modernization, workflow improvement, and business operations experience from Richard Allen.">
<section class="page-intro"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Process Improvement & Business Operations</div><h1>Turn scattered work into repeatable, usable systems.</h1><p class="lede">I’m strongest when a process needs to be documented, simplified, coordinated, measured, governed, tested, or translated into something people can actually use.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container">
  <div class="callout"><strong>Selected proof point:</strong> led a year-long SOP project and project team, creating 100 new SOPs and correcting or standardizing 25+ legacy SOPs.</div>
  <div class="grid two" style="margin-top:1rem">
    <article class="card"><h3>Building an SOP system</h3><p>Created the SOP standards, reviewed and accepted completed work, coached contributors, built a centralized repository, and established guidelines for creating, maintaining, and updating SOPs going forward—not simply a one-time documentation cleanup.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Quality & process control</h3><p>At HawkSoft, investigated a short-call/voicemail workaround affecting multiple representatives, worked through an employee action plan, and helped change QA policy so calls of any length could be reviewed.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Reporting that changed decisions</h3><p>Built recurring management reporting from raw support/call data, analyzed trends, and recommended changes in staffing, training, policies, procedures, and future needs. After an initial period when my manager presented the reports, I personally presented most of the analysis to directors and upper management, and the findings drove operational changes.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Workforce reporting at scale</h3><p>At OHA, managed 400+ position records and maintained 20+ recurring and specialized reports across multiple divisions. Reporting included monthly and specialized work for the CFO area and, at times, the CFO’s superior.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Software validation & release documentation</h3><p>At The Kotter Group, systematically checked new software builds to confirm changes worked as intended and did not break existing functionality, then wrote procedure documentation and created instructional videos for Bridge by Kotter.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Earlier systems modernization</h3><p>At Shady Grove Adventist Hospital, helped replace a DOS-based X-ray film tracking system with a new system, contributing to an approximately 30% efficiency improvement, and helped create the process and procedures used to digitize thousands of X-ray films.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Operational visibility</h3><p>At OED, created a daily activity and claims-tracking process that gave team leadership a clearer view of progress, reporting, and spot checks; also created staff communications and supported queueing, integrity, training, and modernization work.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h3>Supply & warehouse operations</h3><p>At Aramark, managed purchasing and supply operations within a warehouse handling more than $1 million in annual inventory while coordinating receiving, storage, distribution, sanitation, shipping, drivers, and a mixed workforce of roughly 20 people.</p></article>
  </div>
</div></section>
